# Firmware verification workflow

Read `Software Documents/Firmware Development Guidelines.md` and roadmap §3 / §21.

- Continue work packages without blocking on physical board or Renode.
- Software-complete + roadmap WP ticks are OK when build passes and code review standards met.
- Next sequential driver phase (F2–F7) unblocks when current phase is software-complete and entry criteria are met — do not treat open §21 items as a coding blocker.
- Hardware exit criteria without a board → roadmap **§21 Bench verification backlog** (do not tick phase HW exit).
- Prefer host-testable pure logic (scale, parse, CRC) over early Renode models for new sensors.
- F11 (HIL) and F12 (flight readiness) require real hardware; §21 does not substitute for F11.
- Do not invent Renode or "need hardware first" blockers for sequential driver work (F2–F7).
